    "description": "Chicago CBD Data Center is a downtown Chicago carrier-neutral colocation facility operated within the 1547 platform. Its customers include carriers, cloud and content networks, enterprises, and other users that need central-business-district connectivity and access to regional network nodes. The asset follows an asset-heavy digital-infrastructure model based on owned data center real estate, power, cooling, and interconnection infrastructure. Public materials identify the facility at 725 South Wells and emphasize its connectivity to 350 East Cermak and other Chicago network routes. Harrison Street and 1547 acquired the facility in November 2021 as part of a four-asset U.S. data-center transaction; the ownership split is not publicly disclosed. The property remains part of the partners’ connectivity-focused North American data-center portfolio.",
